  "prefLabel": "Rev 601.20 Easement agreement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 601.20 “Easement agreement” means the legal document that identifies the parties involved, identifies the property encumbered by the easement, and describes in detail the public benefit, any renewal terms and all other terms of the easement pursuant to RSA 79-C and RSA 79-D.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Rev 600) #10581, eff 5-1-14; ss by #13916, eff 3-28-24 (formerly Rev 601.21) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Rev 600)",
